    "body": "## Context\nPRD section 13 says: study competitors before M4 to sharpen the differentiator and avoid copying.\n\n## Requirements\n- PRD refs: PRD section 13 (risks)\n\n## Tasks\n- [ ] Review Snyk Agent Scan, mcpproxy-go, Docker MCP tooling, `alexar76/warden`, `mcp-lock`.\n- [ ] For each: scope, offline or not, license, detection approach, rule format, pins/rug-pull support.\n- [ ] List ideas to adopt and ideas to avoid, with credit.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `docs/competitors.md` covers all five tools with a comparison table.\n- [ ] Every claim links a source.\n- [ ] A short section states how mcpmoat differs.\n\n## Notes\nInvariant Labs, tool poisoning: https://invariantlabs.ai/blog/mcp-security-notification-tool-poisoning-attacks\nOWASP MCP Top 10: https://owasp.org/www-project-mcp-top-10/\n\nPick up with the model in the `model:*` label at high effort (see CLAUDE.md).\n",
